{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1486017-help-understanding-injury-conditions","id":1486017,"title":"help Understanding Injury Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-07T18:13:15-07:00","id":1486017,"title":"help Understanding Injury Conditions","content":"Hi! I'm learning the Storypath system in preparation for running an Aberrant game for my group. I'm reading the Trinity Continuum core rulebook and am having trouble understanding how injury conditions work.<br /> <br /> Question #1: On page 106, what do the +1, +2, and +4 represent for Bruised (+1), Injured (+2), and Maimed (+4)?<br /> <br /> Question #2: Does the player get to choose what injury condition they take, regardless of the source of the damage?<br /> <br /> Question #3: Do I, as the Storyteller, determine what the effect the Injury Condition has on a player, using the examples provided on page 107 as a guides?<br /> <br /> Question #4: Am I understanding correctly that Injury Conditions don't stack, that only the highest Injury Complication applies? Is an Injury Complication the same thing as the Effects listed on page 107 under each Injury Condition?<br /> <br /> Sorry for all the questions. I've played lots of D20-based RPGs and the Storypath system seems very fun but I'm having trouble wrapping my head around some of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25223-phdoom","name":"PhDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T19:22:20-07:00","id":1486019,"title":"","content":"1) That's the increased Difficulty the injury imposes to future dice rolls. It may or may not apply to all rolls, depending on the nature of the injury. The Storyguide and player should decide the nature of the injury when it's inflicted. For example, if a Bruised injury condition (+1) is determined to be a sprained ankle, it will apply to the character trying to run or do athletics, but probably won't apply to them sitting at a desk and trying to hack a computer.<br /> <br /> 2) Unless the source of the damage specifies what kind of condition, yes. Some powers stipulate things like inflicting Maimed, so if the character doesn't have a Maimed free, but they still have Bruised and Injured, they're still Taken Out.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes, but the player's input is just as valuable. You don't have to do all the work if your players are helping, but teh Storyguide has final say. (You're not a 'Storyteller' in Storypath, you're a 'Storyguide'.)<br /> <br /> 4) Only apply the highest that's relevant. Building on the example above, the character has a Bruised (+1 - sprained ankle) and an Injured (+2, Minor Concussion). If they're hacking the computer, that's a Mental action and they suffer +2 Difficulty. If they're just trying to run away, the concussion isn't that relevant, but the sprained ankle is, so they suffer +1 Difficulty.<br /> <br /> That's how it works, but if it's too much for you and your players while you're learning the system, you can feel free to not detail the Injury Conditions as characters receive them and just apply the blanket +1/+2/+4 Difficulty to all rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T15:16:34-07:00","id":1486072,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much Bunyip! Your answers cleared up my confusion. I appreciate the quick response <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25223-phdoom","name":"PhDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}